==English==
[[File:Skittles - geograph.org.uk - 153273.jpg|thumb|Skittles - geograph.org.uk - 153273]]

===Etymology===
Origin {{unk|en|title=unknown}}. Perhaps of {{der|en|gmq}} origin, from {{der|en|non|skutill|t=bolt, harpoon}}, related to {{m|non|skjóta|t=to shoot}}, but the OED dismisses this connection as conjecture. The Old Norse word is related to Swedish and {{cog|da|skyttel|t=shuttle, child's toy}}. Compare also {{cog|ang|sċytel|t=a dart, bolt}}. More at {{m|en|shuttle}}.

